<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hoshina Masayuki</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1611–1673</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hoshina Masayuki was a son of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogun</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-hidetada">Tokugawa Hidetada</a> and half-brother of Iemitsu, raised in the Hoshina family. Given <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aizu">Aizu</a> in 1643, he founded the line that held it until 1868, and he served as guardian of the young shogun Ietsuna. His house code bound his descendants to absolute loyalty to the shogunate, which shaped Aizu's stand in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boshin-war">Boshin War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hoshina-masayuki.jpg" alt="Hoshina Masayuki" width="320" height="310" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gameposo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hoshina_Masayuki2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
